{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Calendar",
    "description": "Standard-library calendar templates (esm-spec §9.7.1 template-library file). Nine match-less expression templates give the pure-AST definitions of the datetime.* closed functions (esm-spec §9.2): `year(t)`, `month(t)`, `day(t)`, `hour(t)`, `minute(t)`, `second(t)`, `day_of_year(t)`, `julian_day(t)` and `is_leap_year(t)`, each of one parameter `t`, UTC seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z (binary64, proleptic Gregorian, no leap seconds). Each splits t exactly into the day number d = floor(floor(t) / 86400) and the whole second of the day s = floor(t) - 86400 d, then runs Howard Hinnant's civil_from_days, every integer division written floor(a / b); on the domain |t| < 2^52 s every intermediate is an integer below 2^53, so each floor is exact and each field equals the closed function's value. Outside that domain, and for NaN or an infinite t, every template returns NaN. The second-valued constants are unit-bearing `const` nodes (esm-spec §4.8.5), so t is read in seconds and every field is dimensionless. Import with `expression_template_imports` and invoke with `apply_expression_template`; see docs/content/standard_library.md.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML"],
    "created": "2026-04-25T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": ["standard-library", "calendar", "datetime", "expression-templates"],
    "references": [{"citation": "esm-spec.md §9.2 (datetime.* semantics, the pinned julian_day formula); §9.6 (expression templates); §9.7.1 (template-library files); §4.8.5 (unit-bearing const)."}, {"citation": "Hinnant, H., 2013. chrono-Compatible Low-Level Date Algorithms, `civil_from_days`. https://howardhinnant.github.io/date_algorithms.html"}]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "year": {
      "params": ["t"],
      "description": "Proleptic-Gregorian year of the UTC instant t (seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z), astronomical numbering (0 = 1 BC), the value datetime.year gives (esm-spec §9.2). Howard Hinnant's civil_from_days on the day number d = floor(floor(t) / 86400): era = floor(z / 146097) with z = d + 719468, day of era, year of era, then one year added for January and February. Finite t with |t| < 2^52 s; outside it, and for NaN or an infinite t, the value is NaN (0/0).",
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          {"op": "<", "args": [{"op": "abs", "args": ["t"]}, {"op": "const", "args": [], "value": 4503599627370496, "units": "s"}]},
          {
            "op": "+",
